{{also|ODD|Odd|ödd|o'dd}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|odde}}, {{m|enm|od|t=odd (not even); leftover after division into pairs}}, from {{der|en|non|oddi|t=odd, third or additional number; triangle}}, from {{m|non|oddr|t=point of a weapon}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*uzdaz|t=point}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wes-|t=to stick, prick, pierce, sting}} + {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-|t=to set, place}}. 

Cognate to {{cog|is|oddi|t=triangle, point of land, odd number}}, {{cog|sv|udda|t=odd|sc=Latn}}, {{m|sv|udd|t=a point|sc=Latn}}, {{cog|da|od|t=point of weapon”|sc=Latn}} and {{m|da|odde|t=a headland, point}}, {{cog|nb|odde|t=a point”, “odd”, “peculiar|sc=Latn}}; related to {{cog|ang|ord|t=a point}}. {{doublet|en|ord}} {{gloss|"point"}}.

